                <pb facs="0567" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg493"/>

                <head>No. 3.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—<placeName>Madrid</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-14">February 14</date>—1
                        o’clock p. m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To American Minister at Lisbon;</hi></p>
                <p>For God’s sake get the Sacramento off immediately. The Stonewall will be ready to
                    sail tomorrow. A second steamer under English flag has just entered Ferrol. Very
                    suspicious. Supposed consort of the Stonewall. The Niagara watches both.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>PERRY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
